@startuml OpenFinder_Startup_Recovery
title OpenFinder Durable Startup and Recovery
skinparam shadowing false

participant "OpenFinderApp" as Main
participant "ApplicationServices" as Services
database "AppDatabase" as DB
participant "PersistenceMaintenance" as Maintenance
participant "TaskHandlerRegistry" as Registry
participant "TaskQueueService" as Queue
participant "AppModel" as Model

Main -> Services: create composition root(tasks.sqlite)
Services -> DB: open and validate schema

alt database unavailable, malformed, or from future
  DB --> Services: safe failure (database preserved)
  Services --> Model: readiness = unavailable
else database ready
  DB --> Services: schema v3 ready
  Services -> Maintenance: reconcile artifacts and task effects
  Maintenance -> DB: roll forward durable states
  Services -> Registry: compose exact handler/payload versions
  Registry --> Services: validated registry
  Services -> Queue: installHandlerRegistry
  Services -> DB: load descriptors, records, logs
  Services -> Queue: recoverPersistedTasks
  Services -> Queue: resumeRecoveredTasks
  Queue --> Model: readiness = ready + task projection
end

note over DB,Queue
Queued work never starts before database,
reconciliation, and exact handler registration succeed.
end note

note over Maintenance
Recovery is roll-forward.
No database deletion or silent recreation.
end note
@enduml
